WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.746
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.746 --> 00:00:04.778
- [Voiceover] Stepping onto Socotra Island

00:00:04.778 --> 00:00:08.488
is like setting foot
on an alien landscape.

00:00:08.488 --> 00:00:10.724
This place is one of the
most isolated landforms

00:00:10.724 --> 00:00:12.066
on Earth.

00:00:12.066 --> 00:00:14.831
Located in the Arabian
Sea, south of Yemen,

00:00:14.831 --> 00:00:17.000
the island separated from
the mainland of Africa

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.333
between six and seven million years ago.

00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:26.399
There are nearly 700
endemic species on Socotra

00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:30.385
that are found nowhere else on the planet.

00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:32.910
Perhaps the most head-turning 
of Socotra's species

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.149
is the dragon's blood tree.

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:38.647
These strange umbrella
shaped trees dot the island.

00:00:38.647 --> 00:00:41.328
Its top-heavy design is
actually an adaptation

00:00:41.328 --> 00:00:43.202
to Socotra's arid climate.

00:00:43.202 --> 00:00:45.601
The large green crown provides shade

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:47.428
which reduces evaporation in a place

00:00:47.428 --> 00:00:50.095
that sees very little rainfall.

00:00:51.413 --> 00:00:53.730
This otherworldly gem
has experienced threats

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.215
to its ecology from human development.

00:00:56.215 --> 00:00:59.231
But the United Nations stepped in in 2008

00:00:59.231 --> 00:01:02.398
designating it a UNESCO heritage site.

